ts (compile error if anyone imports it)\\n- [ ] All deprecated exports removed\\n- [ ] Public surface matches CONTRACT-001 + nothing else\\n- [ ] CHANGELOG.md documents the breaking change\",\"claimed-at\":\"2026-04-19T23:35:53Z\",\"claimed-machine\":\"eitri\",\"claimed-pid\":\"721226\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-18T21:26:10.996811519Z\",\"description\":\"Cutover release. Delete legacy agentlib.Run, all the legacy provider/compactor/tool/prompt/session exports. Internal/ enforcement blocks any external consumer that hasnt migrated.\\n\\nPre-conditions:\\n- DDx fully migrated (DDx tracker epic complete)\\n- All HELIX/Dun consumers (if any) migrated\\n- Internal/ move bead landed (agent-X)\\n- Glob→find rename landed\\n\\nTag v0.5.0. Update CHANGELOG with breaking-change notes.\",\"events\":[{\"actor\":\"ddx\",\"body\":\"{\\\"resolved_provider\\\":\\\"agent\\\",\\\"resolved_model\\\":\\\"qwen3.5-27b\\\",\\\"fallback_chain\\\":[]}\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-19T23:36:02.576302246Z\",\"kind\":\"routing\",\"source\":\"ddx agent execute-bead\",\"summary\":\"provider=agent model=qwen3.5-27b\"},{\"actor\":\"ddx\",\"body\":\"tier=cheap harness=agent model=qwen3.5-27b probe=ok\\nmodel \\\"qwen3.5-27b\\\" is not in the catalog and no discovered provider serves it\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-19T23:36:02.614245139Z\",\"kind\":\"tier-attempt\",\"source\":\"ddx agent execute-loop\",\"summary\":\"execution_failed\"}],\"execute-loop-heartbeat-at\":\"2026-04-19T23:35:53.359453202Z\",\"id\":\"agent-52bcd4c3\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"phase:build\",\"kind:release\"],\"owner\":\"ddx\",\"parent\":\"agent-a770e781\",\"priority\":0,\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"title\":\"release: tag agent v0.5.0 (legacy gone; internal/-enforced minimal surface)\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-19T23:36:02.629217171Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:108:{\"acceptance\":\"- [ ] DdxAgent.Execute exists and matches CONTRACT-001 signature\\n- [ ] All three timeout knobs work independently with documented semantics\\n- [ ] StallPolicy default + explicit configurations both enforced; emits stall event before termination\\n- [ ] Orphan-model error is explicit and surfaces as Status=failed\\n- [ ] Provider-deadline wrapping classifies failover-eligible vs not per existing model\\n- [ ] Per-model context_length resolved from provider API \\u003e catalog \\u003e default\\n- [ ] Metadata stamps both events and session-log lines (verified by test)\\n- [ ] SessionLogDir override directs logs to specified path\\n- [ ] OS-level cancel test passes (ctx.Done() during streaming)\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"a89aedb44572f67e5ec0e6a576d0b7f625a66907\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-18T21:22:51.416988858Z\",\"description\":\"Implement DdxAgent.Execute as the primary verb. Wraps existing agent loop. Internal-only details:\\n\\n- Per-model context-window resolution using existing modelcatalog.ContextWindowForModel + provider /api lookup (supersedes agent-6f8caa00 and agent-8682793b — close those when this lands).\\n- StallPolicy enforcement: ReadOnlyTools + NoopCompactions limits end execution with Status=stalled.\\n- Three timeout knobs: Timeout (wall-clock), IdleTimeout (activity-quiet), ProviderTimeout (per-HTTP).\\n- Orphan-model validation: Model set + no provider has it + no catalog entry → Status=failed with explicit error.\\n- Provider-deadline wrapping: every HTTP call wrapped; transport/auth/upstream failures eligible for failover; prompt/tool errors not.\\n- Route-reason attribution: start-event routing_decision includes the reason string.\\n- OS-level subprocess cleanup: ctx.Done() reaps PTY/orphan processes (matters more for subprocess harnesses in Phase 3, but the hook lives here).\\n- Metadata is bidirectional: stamps every emitted event AND every session-log line.\\n- SessionLogDir per-request override.\\n\\nReturns \\u003c-chan Event closed when execution terminates. Final event carries status, usage, cost, session log path, optional message history, routing_actual.\",\"id\":\"agent-755fea77\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"phase:build\",\"area:execution\",\"area:contract\"],\"parent\":\"agent-a770e781\",\"priority\":1,\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"service: implement DdxAgent.Execute over native providers (with StallPolicy, three timeouts, contract behaviors)\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-18T22:29:32.27811736Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:111:{\"acceptance\":\"- [ ] DdxAgent.RouteStatus(ctx) returns RouteStatusReport with all routes from config\\n- [ ] Each RouteStatusEntry shows candidates with health, cooldown, recent latency, success rate\\n- [ ] LastDecision cache populated for recently-resolved routes\\n- [ ] Test exercises a route under cooldown\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"5ab5509220616fc5c649291ed66f0028437b4982\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-18T21:24:50.235591538Z\",\"description\":\"Implement DdxAgent.RouteStatus(ctx) per CONTRACT-001. Returns RouteStatusReport aggregating cooldown state, recent decisions cache, observation-derived per-(provider,model) latency. Distinct from per-request ResolveRoute — this is the read-only operator dashboard view.\\n\\nBacked by the same routing engine state ResolveRoute consults (port from DDx routing_metrics.go + routing_signals.go).\\n\\nPowers the DDx-side ddx agent route-status command after migration.\",\"id\":\"agent-763ae08b\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"phase:build\",\"area:contract\",\"area:routing\"],\"parent\":\"agent-a770e781\",\"priority\":1,\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"service: implement DdxAgent.RouteStatus (operator dashboard surface)\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-18T22:49:24.976771495Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:119:{\"acceptance\":\"- [ ] CONTRACT-001 file exists with all 7 method signatures, all input/output types, all event shapes, all named behaviors\\n- [ ] No \\\"TBD\\\" or \\\"TODO\\\" in the contract\\n- [ ] Reviewed by at least one independent reader against the source plan\",\"claimed-at\":\"2026-04-18T21:38:45Z\",\"claimed-machine\":\"eitri\",\"claimed-pid\":\"77012\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"1264bc897d5b74b46749743bfab940d0e5534210\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-18T21:22:05.901408458Z\",\"description\":\"Write docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-001-ddx-agent-service.md verbatim from the contract draft in /Users/erik/Projects/ddx/tmp-plan or current working copy. Contents: DdxAgent interface (7 methods: Execute, TailSessionLog, ListHarnesses, ListProviders, ListModels, HealthCheck, ResolveRoute, RouteStatus); input/output types (ExecuteRequest with three timeout knobs + StallPolicy + SessionLogDir + Metadata bidirectional + PreResolved; ExecuteResponse with routing_actual; RouteRequest, RouteDecision, RouteStatusReport with cooldowns; HarnessInfo/ProviderInfo/ModelInfo with rich fields; HealthTarget polymorphic; FakeProvider + three assertion hooks for test seams); Event JSON shapes (text_delta, tool_call, tool_result, compaction, routing_decision, stall, final-with-routing_actual); contract-named behaviors (orphan-model validation, provider-deadline wrapping, route-reason attribution, stall detection, compaction-stuck breaking, OS-level subprocess cleanup). Closes with: \\\"this is the entire external surface; anything not here is internal; consumers ask for changes via PR against this doc.\\\" Blocks every other bead in this epic.\",\"execute-loop-heartbeat-at\":\"2026-04-18T21:38:45.064565258Z\",\"id\":\"agent-80c7f8be\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"phase:design\",\"kind:spec\",\"area:contract\"],\"notes\":\"CONTRACT-003-ddx-agent-service.md written and committed (1264bc8). Slot taken: existing CONTRACT-001 (otel-telemetry-capture) is unrelated, so the new doc is CONTRACT-003. CONTRACT-002 (entanglement) gets deleted by agent-5892857e.\",\"owner\":\"erik\",\"parent\":\"agent-a770e781\",\"priority\":0,\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"contract: write CONTRACT-001-ddx-agent-service.md (the sole external-surface authority)\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-18T21:41:27.375415662Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:122:{\"acceptance\":\"- [ ] internal/execution/deadline.go (or equivalent) implements wall-clock + idle + per-request deadlines\\n- [ ] All three timeout knobs are independently configurable per Execute call\\n- [ ] ErrProviderRequestTimeout (or successor) classified as failover-eligible by routing engine\\n- [ ] provider_deadline_test.go cases pass against the new code\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"a94a1f64eaae6331de31cae2e4e982b0723a5096\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-18T21:25:04.079104959Z\",\"description\":\"Port /Users/erik/Projects/ddx/cli/internal/agent/provider_deadline.go (deadline wrapping logic) into agent internal/execution/. Three timeout knobs (Timeout, IdleTimeout, ProviderTimeout) all enforced internally per CONTRACT-001.\\n\\nExisting wrapProviderWithDeadlines / timeoutProvider / streamingTimeoutProvider patterns get rebuilt as internal middleware around the provider call sites. ErrProviderRequestTimeout becomes an internal error that the routing engine sees for failover classification.\\n\\nTests (provider_deadline_test.go, 188 lines) port to assert against the new internal API — likely a mechanical rewrite, not verbatim.\",\"id\":\"agent-858f76c4\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"phase:build\",\"area:execution\",\"kind:port\"],\"parent\":\"agent-a770e781\",\"priority\":2,\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"execution: port provider_deadline.go semantics into internal/execution/\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-18T22:05:24.256409541Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:132:{\"acceptance\":\"Result, session artifacts, and telemetry include requested model/ref, route key, selected provider, resolved model, attempt chain, and failover count; existing usage/cost semantics remain correct; DDx can consume attribution fields without reading provider candidate config; tests cover successful routing, failover, and direct-provider override paths.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-10T19:32:37.427609506Z\",\"dependencies\":[{\"issue_id\":\"agent-8a72585b\",\"depends_on_id\":\"agent-a82ab304\",\"type\":\"blocks\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-10T19:33:11Z\"}],\"description\":\"Update result/session/telemetry surfaces so the embedded runtime exposes DDx-consumable routing facts without leaking inner provider-candidate tables. Record requested model input, requested model_ref when present, route key, selected provider, resolved concrete model, attempted providers, and failover count in Result, session start/end records, and OTel-aligned telemetry. Preserve existing provider/cost attribution semantics. Do not require DDx to understand model_routes or candidate priority state; DDx only needs intent plus outcome attribution so it can combine embedded-harness evidence with its own cross-harness routing data. Background: DDx SD-015 explicitly says DDx must not duplicate embedded provider selection, but it does need the embedded runtime to surface the provider actually chosen.\",\"id\":\"agent-8a72585b\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"helix\",\"phase:build\",\"kind:feature\",\"area:lib\",\"area:telemetry\"],\"parent\":\"agent-f4065aa8\",\"priority\":1,\"spec-id\":\"docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-001-otel-telemetry-capture.md\",\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"Record model-route attribution in results, sessions, and telemetry\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-10T20:08:05.488390829Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:139:{\"acceptance\":\"1. Provider (or equivalent resolved-config struct) exposes a DetectedFlavor() accessor returning a string matching one of the known flavor values (or empty when indeterminate).\\n\\n2. The accessor reads from the cached probe result — no HTTP call on every invocation.\\n\\n3. If ProviderConfig.Flavor was set explicitly, DetectedFlavor() returns that value unchanged (caller-set wins over probe).\\n\\n4. Unit test: probe returns 'omlx' signal -\\u003e Provider.DetectedFlavor() returns 'omlx'. ProviderConfig.Flavor='lmstudio' + probe says 'omlx' -\\u003e DetectedFlavor() returns 'lmstudio'.\\n\\n5. CHANGELOG.md entry describing the new accessor.\",\"claimed-at\":\"2026-04-18T01:40:17Z\",\"claimed-machine\":\"eitri\",\"claimed-pid\":\"1635356\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-18T01:22:17.516353249Z\",\"description\":\"## Context\\n\\nv0.3.11 introduced ProviderConfig.Flavor (lmstudio | omlx | openrouter | ollama) with probe-based autodetection when the field is absent. The probe hits /v1/models/status and /api/v0/models to figure out which flavor the endpoint speaks.\\n\\nDownstream consumers (DDx at DocumentDrivenDX/ddx, specifically the autorouting plan under ddx-2d974641 and the capability-gating bead ddx-4817edfd) need to know which flavor the library decided on for each configured provider — so their own routing/scoring/diagnostics can say 'this provider is omlx-flavor, so tool schemas go through auto-translation' without repeating the probe.\\n\\nToday this is not exposed via the public API. Downstream has two choices:\\n1. Re-run the same probe independently. Wastes the library's work and can produce different answers if servers flap.\\n2. Hard-code assumptions based on port numbers or URL patterns. Fragile — exactly the heuristic v0.3.11 replaced.\\n\\n## Ask\\n\\nExpose a getter on the resolved Provider (post-Load, post-detect) that returns the effective flavor:\\n\\n    // DetectedFlavor returns the flavor the runtime is using for this provider.\\n    // If ProviderConfig.Flavor was set explicitly, returns that value. Otherwise\\n    // returns the auto-detected flavor from the startup probe. Empty string when\\n    // the probe was inconclusive or the provider is not a supported flavor-family.\\n    func (p *Provider) DetectedFlavor() string\\n\\nCache the probe result so DetectedFlavor is a cheap lookup, not a fresh HTTP call.\\n\\n## Use case\\n\\nDDx uses this to:\\n- Tag routing events with the effective flavor so debugging is self-contained in execution evidence.\\n- Feed capability gating (supports_tools, supports_structured_output) off the flavor in scoring.\\n- Generate human-readable 'ddx agent check --verbose' output showing each provider's flavor.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n- Exposing the RAW probe results (HTTP responses). Only the distilled flavor.\\n- Making the flavor mutable at runtime. Providers are loaded + detected once per process.\",\"execute-loop-heartbeat-at\":\"2026-04-18T01:40:17.954331827Z\",\"id\":\"agent-92f0f324\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"agent\",\"kind:enhancement\",\"area:provider\",\"area:api\"],\"notes\":\"Fresh-eyes review 2026-04-18: Provider already has a flavor-adjacent field — providerSystem (URL-heuristic from openAIIdentity, stored at New() time). It's used on 4 hot paths: AttemptMetadata.ProviderSystem, openRouterCostAttribution, ProviderIdentity(), and streaming attempt metadata. Those fire every response and cannot afford a network probe. DetectedFlavor() must layer on top: return explicit Config.Flavor if set, otherwise cached probe result via sync.Once, otherwise fall back to providerSystem. Do NOT migrate the 4 hot callsites off providerSystem in this bead — that's a telemetry contract change (CONTRACT-001) and scope creep. Docstring must explicitly document the two-path layering: DetectedFlavor() for pre-dispatch gating (probe-confirmed); ProviderIdentity() for per-response telemetry (eager, non-blocking).\",\"owner\":\"erik\",\"priority\":2,\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"expose Provider.DetectedFlavor() so downstream tools can introspect probe result without re-probing\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-18T01:57:30.690987048Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:147:{\"acceptance\":\"- [ ] DdxAgent.TailSessionLog(ctx, sessionID) returns \\u003c-chan Event closed when session completes\\n- [ ] Subscriber attached mid-execution receives all subsequent events\\n- [ ] Subscriber attached after completion receives the final event then channel closes\\n- [ ] Multiple subscribers on the same sessionID each receive full streams\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"bbb01c24cf5eb15e2ae11c37c207bf79feb2aac6\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-18T21:24:56.709043765Z\",\"description\":\"Implement DdxAgent.TailSessionLog(ctx, sessionID) per CONTRACT-001. Streams events from a previously-started or in-progress session by ID. Used by DDx workers/UI to subscribe to a run started elsewhere (server-managed worker that DDx CLI wants to follow).\\n\\nBacked by the same internal session-log writer Execute uses. Multi-subscriber-safe: multiple TailSessionLog callers on the same sessionID each get the full event stream.\\n\\nReplaces DDx-side session_log_tailer.go (109 lines) which currently tails the JSONL file directly.\",\"id\":\"agent-99d2a84c\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"phase:build\",\"area:contract\",\"area:execution\"],\"parent\":\"agent-a770e781\",\"priority\":1,\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"service: implement DdxAgent.TailSessionLog (subscribe to in-progress session events)\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-18T22:36:34.44262041Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:159:{\"acceptance\":\"- [ ] CONTRACT-001-ddx-agent-service.md is the sole external-surface authority on the agent side\\n- [ ] DdxAgent Service interface exposes 7 methods (Execute, TailSessionLog, ListHarnesses, ListProviders, ListModels, HealthCheck, ResolveRoute, RouteStatus) with the input/output types specified in the plan\\n- [ ] All five subprocess harnesses (claude, codex, opencode, pi, gemini) are ported into agent internal/harnesses/ with behavioral parity tests\\n- [ ] Native agent harness wins on at least one batch noninteractive task in the integration suite\\n- [ ] All entanglement docs deleted (CONTRACT-002 in agent; SD-015, SD-015-resolution-path-trace, SD-023, plan-2026-04-08 in DDx)\\n- [ ] Internal/ tree blocks external imports of compaction, prompt, tool, session, observations, modelcatalog, provider/* (compile-time enforcement)\\n- [ ] DDx imports nothing from agent except the root agentlib package\\n- [ ] Integration suite runs across all available harnesses with cost cap and determinism controls\\n- [ ] All six \\\"badly implemented\\\" routing smells fixed structurally, not patched\\n- [ ] agent v0.4.0-pre tagged (legacy + new contract); v0.5.0 tagged (legacy gone, internal/ enforced)\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-18T21:21:28.726590048Z\",\"description\":\"Consolidate LLM routing + harness orchestration entirely into ddx-agent. The module becomes the one stop shop for optimally routed one-shot noninteractive agentic prompts. Two roles: (1) direct first-class agent over native providers (bragi, vidar, openrouter, anthropic), designed to win at batch noninteractive; (2) wrapper around subprocess agents (claude, codex, opencode, pi, gemini) for convenience and cost management.\\n\\nDDx becomes a thin Service consumer with no agent-internal imports. The boundary is one Go interface (DdxAgent, 7 methods) defined in CONTRACT-001. Internal packages move under internal/ — compiler-enforced.\\n\\nReplaces the spec entanglement that produced the six well-documented routing smells (parallel routing engines, --provider bypass, fragmented fuzzy match, profile-vs-failover split, capability gating asymmetry, health/quota fragmentation). Plan: /tmp/ddx-agent-service-interface-plan.md (in DDx repo for reference).\\n\\nCross-tracker: paired with DDx epic for the consumer-side migration. Beads in this epic precede each corresponding DDx bead.\",\"id\":\"agent-a770e781\",\"issue_type\":\"epic\",\"labels\":[\"phase:design\",\"area:contract\",\"area:lib\",\"kind:architecture\"],\"priority\":0,\"status\":\"open\",\"title\":\"Epic: ddx-agent owns LLM execution + routing — single Service contract, harnesses ported, internal/-enforced boundary\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-18T21:21:28.726590048Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:167:{\"acceptance\":\"- [ ] ListModels with empty filter returns models from every healthy provider+harness\\n- [ ] ListModels with Provider=\\\"bragi\\\" returns only bragi models, with full metadata populated\\n- [ ] IsConfigured/IsDefault flags are accurate\\n- [ ] CatalogRef is non-empty when the catalog recognizes the model\\n- [ ] RankPosition reflects the latest discovery ranking\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"32f1d51b1bebd6f23a99243de40b414d9ad6d803\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-18T21:24:24.097700908Z\",\"description\":\"Implement DdxAgent.ListModels(ctx, ModelFilter) per CONTRACT-001. Returns []ModelInfo where each entry includes:\\n- ID, Provider, Harness\\n- ContextLength (resolved: provider API \\u003e catalog \\u003e default)\\n- Capabilities []string\\n- Cost (from catalog)\\n- PerfSignal (observation-derived latency / throughput / success-rate)\\n- Available\\n- IsConfigured (matches an explicit model_routes entry)\\n- IsDefault (matches the configured default model)\\n- CatalogRef (canonical catalog reference if recognized)\\n- RankPosition (ordinal in the latest discovery rank for this provider; -1 if unranked)\\n\\nFilter: {Harness, Provider} — empty filter = all models across all harnesses + providers. Filter applied internally; clients dont post-filter.\\n\\nLive discovery + catalog merge happens inside this method; clients never see raw provider /v1/models.\",\"id\":\"agent-ac0c3a9b\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"phase:build\",\"area:contract\",\"area:routing\"],\"parent\":\"agent-a770e781\",\"priority\":1,\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"service: implement DdxAgent.ListModels with full metadata (cost, perf, capabilities, ranking)\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-18T22:23:28.49381205Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:183:{\"acceptance\":\"A telemetry package exists with a stable runtime interface, a no-op implementation, and OTel span scaffolding for invoke_agent/chat/execute_tool; export failures are best-effort and do not fail runs; unit tests cover basic span lifecycle and no-op behavior\",\"claimed-at\":\"2026-04-10T00:24:17Z\",\"claimed-machine\":\"eitri\",\"claimed-pid\":\"3343400\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"57e3978600fbc45e4cd40e13a63fb76bde456676\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-09T21:37:12.617653775Z\",\"dependencies\":[{\"issue_id\":\"agent-bb6aad8a\",\"depe