 least one demonstration test in agent repo\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"2b089c69082f175b35dbfef683769b625b99c67a\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-18T21:22:35.128700018Z\",\"description\":\"Implement the four test-injection seams from CONTRACT-001. All guarded by \\\"//go:build testseam\\\" so production binaries cannot construct them.\\n\\n1. FakeProvider — three patterns (Static script, Dynamic callback, InjectError per-call). Replaces the existing virtual.New/InlineResponse seam used in 32 DDx test sites today.\\n2. PromptAssertionHook(systemPrompt, userPrompt, contextFiles) — observe constructed prompts.\\n3. CompactionAssertionHook(messagesBefore, messagesAfter, tokensFreed) — observe real compactions only (no-ops never delivered).\\n4. ToolWiringHook(harness, toolNames) — observe resolved tool list per Execute.\\n\\nWire all four into Options. Tests: each seam exercised by at least one unit test in the agent repo, demonstrating it captures what it should.\",\"id\":\"agent-ef5a50d0\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"phase:build\",\"kind:testing\",\"area:contract\"],\"parent\":\"agent-a770e781\",\"priority\":1,\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"service: implement four test seams (FakeProvider + PromptAssertionHook + CompactionAssertionHook + ToolWiringHook)\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-18T22:00:55.425934436Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:249:{\"acceptance\":\"Tests covering AC-FEAT-005-05 and AC-FEAT-005-06 exist and prove table/JSON/CSV usage output, known-vs-unknown cost preservation, and best-effort behavior when logging or telemetry export fails; ok  \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/cmd/ddx-agent\\t(cached)\\nok  \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/session\\t(cached)\\nok  \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/telemetry\\t(cached)\\nok  \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent\\t(cached)\\nok  \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/compaction\\t(cached)\\nok  \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/config\\t(cached)\\nok  \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/eval/navigation\\t(cached)\\n?   \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/internal/compactionctx\\t[no test files]\\n?   \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/internal/safefs\\t[no test files]\\nok  \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/modelcatalog\\t(cached)\\nok  \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/occompat\\t(cached)\\nok  \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/picompat\\t(cached)\\nok  \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/prompt\\t(cached)\\nok  \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/provider/anthropic\\t(cached)\\nok  \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/provider/openai\\t(cached)\\nok  \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/provider/virtual\\t(cached)\\n?   \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/scripts\\t[no test files]\\nok  \\tgithub.com/DocumentDrivenDX/agent/tool\\t(cached) passes.\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-10T15:53:59.813541815Z\",\"description\":\"\\u003ccontext-digest\\u003e\\n\\u003cprinciples\\u003eReporting surfaces are part of the contract, not optional polish · Best-effort observability semantics need end-to-end tests at the run/CLI boundary\\u003c/principles\\u003e\\n\\u003cconcerns\\u003eusage output formats | unknown-cost accounting | log/telemetry failure resilience\\u003c/concerns\\u003e\\n\\u003cpractices\\u003eUse seeded session logs for deterministic usage tests and temp dirs/mock exporters for failure-path tests · Prefer end-to-end assertions over unit-only coverage here\\u003c/practices\\u003e\\n\\u003cadrs\\u003eADR-001 and CONTRACT-001\\u003c/adrs\\u003e\\n\\u003cgoverning\\u003eFEAT-005 AC-FEAT-005-05 and AC-FEAT-005-06\\u003c/governing\\u003e\\n\\u003c/context-digest\\u003e\\n\\nTelemetry conformance is well-covered, but the user-facing reporting and resilience edges are not. Add tests that:\\n- prove `ddx-agent usage` supports every documented output mode, including CSV, while preserving known-cost vs unknown-cost semantics and time-window filtering\\n- prove unwritable log directories or telemetry export failures do not abort a successful run, emit an operator-visible warning, and leave any partial artifacts readable\\n- where appropriate, assert that correlation metadata survives through both session start and session end so replay/usage tools can attribute runs consistently\\n\\nRelevant files: `cmd/ddx-agent/usage_cli_test.go`, `session/logger_test.go`, `telemetry/telemetry_test.go`, and CLI/session integration helpers.\",\"id\":\"agent-f2b590db\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"helix\",\"phase:test\",\"kind:testing\",\"area:telemetry\"],\"notes\":\"Superseded by agent-010074fa after shell-quoting corruption in the first batch bead-creation pass.\",\"parent\":\"agent-42d295a3\",\"priority\":1,\"spec-id\":\"docs/helix/01-frame/features/FEAT-005-logging-and-cost.md\",\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"Add reporting and observability-resilience tests for usage output modes and best-effort failures\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-10T15:56:08.736397107Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:265:{\"acceptance\":\"- [ ] Session log of a 100% no-op-compaction execution contains zero compaction events\\n- [ ] Real compactions still emit events with the same data shape (messages_before, messages_after, tokens_freed)\\n- [ ] Test asserts the suppression at default verbosity\",\"claimed-at\":\"2026-04-18T21:52:39Z\",\"claimed-machine\":\"eitri\",\"claimed-pid\":\"82652\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"e707dafd7a23ec20b42310d44f1d13fd0aa06b81\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-18T21:22:56.545926812Z\",\"description\":\"Per CONTRACT-001 event schema: type=compaction events fire ONLY when actual work was performed (messages_after \\u003c messages_before OR token count drops). No-op compactions emit nothing at default verbosity.\\n\\nExisting agent-22c95151 documents the original need; this bead is the realization in the new contract context. Close agent-22c95151 when this lands.\",\"execute-loop-heartbeat-at\":\"2026-04-18T21:52:39.455443399Z\",\"id\":\"agent-fbc6b277\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"phase:build\",\"area:compaction\",\"kind:telemetry\"],\"notes\":\"Suppression already in place at /Users/erik/Projects/agent/loop.go:145-147 (early-return when compactor signals no-op via (msgs, nil, nil)). The events the user observed earlier in this session were against the alpha22 binary which predated this fix. This bead adds a regression test (e707daf) to guard against the suppression being removed in future refactors.\\n\\nCross-ref: CONTRACT-003 specifies \\\"type=compaction events fire ONLY when actual work was performed\\\" as a named behavior. Test asserts this end-to-end via Callback inspection.\\n\\nCloses ddx-side bead noted as superseding agent-22c95151.\",\"owner\":\"erik\",\"parent\":\"agent-a770e781\",\"priority\":2,\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"compaction: suppress no-op compaction telemetry (supersedes agent-22c95151)\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-18T21:56:08.567475435Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:280:{\"acceptance\":\"Streaming timing uses real delta arrival timestamps rather than subtracting cumulative callback time; a regression test with callback sleep plus inter-delta provider delay verifies ddx.timing.generation_ms still includes the provider delay and EventLLMDelta timestamps remain monotonic.\",\"claimed-at\":\"2026-04-10T01:44:09Z\",\"claimed-machine\":\"eitri\",\"claimed-pid\":\"3948379\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"863eecb98d4dcca506fdb42a6a67864410c38442\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-10T01:42:19.102557411Z\",\"description\":\"Review finding from fresh-eyes review.\\nFile: stream_consume.go:44\\nCategory: correctness\\nSeverity: medium\\nDescription: consumeStream now computes each delta timestamp as time.Now().Add(-callbackDelay) and grows callbackDelay by the duration of prior EventLLMDelta callbacks. When a later streamed delta becomes ready while an earlier callback is still running, this subtracts both observer latency and real provider generation time that elapsed during that callback. In the shipped providers, ChatStream uses a single-slot channel, so later deltas can queue behind the consumer and then be back-dated when read. That makes ddx.timing.generation_ms and delta event timestamps too small or even flat across distinct arrivals, which violates CONTRACT-001's requirement that timing reflect the streamed output window rather than an adjusted observer schedule.\\nSuggested fix: Capture an arrival timestamp at the producer or carry it on StreamDelta so consumeStream can use actual delta arrival times. At minimum, add a regression test that combines callback sleep with real delayBetween timing and verifies generation_ms still includes the provider delay that elapsed while the callback was running.\",\"id\":\"hx-1fcb3c84\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"helix\",\"phase:build\",\"review-finding\"],\"owner\":\"erik\",\"priority\":0,\"spec-id\":\"stream_consume.go\",\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"correctness: callback-delay compensation undercounts real stream generation\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-10T01:45:22.728662476Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:285:{\"acceptance\":\"A session whose chat spans all have known cost preserves a root invoke_agent ddx.cost.amount equal to the sum of child costs even when provenance differs across turns; the root span only emits ddx.cost.source=unknown when at least one contributing chat span has unknown cost; automated tests cover mixed provider-reported/configured cost rollups.\",\"claimed-at\":\"2026-04-10T04:17:15Z\",\"claimed-machine\":\"eitri\",\"claimed-pid\":\"517258\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"c083df5f46fe37557b8feedf66af32013a0a9e35\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-10T04:02:07.463686182Z\",\"description\":\"Review finding from fresh-eyes review.\\nFile: loop.go:289\\nCategory: correctness\\nSeverity: medium\\nDescription: The new root-span cost rollup logic marks the invoke_agent span as unknown whenever known child chat spans disagree on ddx.cost.source, currency, or pricing_ref. That drops a valid total for mixed but fully known sessions, which violates CONTRACT-001's rule that the root cost only becomes unknown when a contributing chat span has unknown cost. Reproduced against the current code by running a two-turn session with a provider-reported first turn and an exact configured-cost second turn: result.CostUSD=0.03 while the root span still emits ddx.cost.source=unknown.\\nSuggested fix: Roll up root ddx.cost.amount whenever every contributing chat span has known cost, and only force ddx.cost.source=unknown when a contributing span is actually unknown. If metadata such as pricing_ref or source cannot be represented cleanly at the root, omit or summarize those fields rather than discarding the known total. Add a regression test covering mixed known-cost provenance across turns.\",\"id\":\"hx-264e7ea0\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"helix\",\"phase:build\",\"review-finding\"],\"owner\":\"erik\",\"priority\":0,\"spec-id\":\"loop.go\",\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"correctness: preserve known root cost rollups across mixed known cost sources\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-10T04:18:57.184174548Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:289:{\"acceptance\":\"All review passes complete; findings filed as beads; AGENTS.md updated if needed\",\"claimed-at\":\"2026-04-09T21:52:07Z\",\"claimed-machine\":\"eitri\",\"claimed-pid\":\"1812475\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"de8c772d6d6cd70071b4300358036507051cbea2\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-09T21:51:41.579701497Z\",\"description\":\"\\u003ccontext-digest\\u003e\\u003cprinciples\\u003eDesign for Change · Design for Simplicity · Validate Your Work · Make Intent Explicit · Prefer Reversible Decisions\\u003c/principles\\u003e\\u003cconcerns\\u003ego-std | testing\\u003c/concerns\\u003e\\u003cpractices\\u003eUse Go stdlib toolchain with testing+testify; verify runtime/provider changes against streaming and retry behavior; review target is last commit de8c772 for agent-2f548733 against CONTRACT-001.\\u003c/practices\\u003e\\u003cgoverning\\u003eFresh-eyes review of last commit de8c772 (agent-2f548733) covering runtime retry ownership and att