` cost as unknown when child chat spans have mixed known provenance. In a clean worktree at commit 5f14aaa, `go test ./...` fails because telemetry_contract_test.go expects the root span to carry ddx.cost.amount=0.03, while a standalone reproduction shows the ended root span still exports only ddx.cost.source=unknown. That leaves the implementation out of sync with the amended contract and keeps the original telemetry bug unfixed.\\nSuggested fix: Update the root-session cost rollup logic in loop.go so mixed known provenance preserves ddx.cost.amount while omitting only the unstable provenance fields (ddx.cost.source, ddx.cost.currency, ddx.cost.pricing_ref) as CONTRACT-001 now requires. Keep the new conformance test green with go test ./... in a clean worktree.\",\"id\":\"hx-cacc76f6\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"helix\",\"phase:build\",\"review-finding\"],\"owner\":\"erik\",\"priority\":0,\"spec-id\":\"loop.go\",\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"correctness: mixed-provenance root cost rollup still exports unknown\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-10T04:34:13.786934256Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:377:{\"acceptance\":\"When any contributing attempt has unknown cost provenance, session.end omits cost_usd instead of emitting -1; replay/session parsing distinguishes omitted cost from zero-cost local cost; regression tests cover both known-cost and unknown-cost session rollups.\",\"claimed-at\":\"2026-04-09T22:13:53Z\",\"claimed-machine\":\"eitri\",\"claimed-pid\":\"1968732\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"0fd0aca909b39909db31ad74954f81e271c80174\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-09T22:12:30.075052671Z\",\"description\":\"Review finding from fresh-eyes review.\\nFile: loop.go:360, loop_test.go:506, session/event.go:52, session/replay.go:108\\nCategory: correctness\\nSeverity: medium\\nDescription: The last-commit fix removed DefaultPricing fallback from per-attempt telemetry, but the session rollup still serializes a numeric cost on every session.end event by copying result.CostUSD unconditionally. When any contributing attempt has unknown provenance, result.CostUSD becomes -1, so session.end now emits `cost_usd: -1` instead of omitting the amount. That still violates CONTRACT-001 and SD-001, which require unknown rollup cost amounts to be omitted. The new regression test in loop_test.go also codifies unconditional session.end cost emission, so a contract-compliant fix would currently fail tests. Downstream session consumers compound the issue because SessionEndData uses a plain float64 and Replay treats zero as `$0 (local)`, so omitted cost cannot be represented distinctly from free local execution.\\nSuggested fix: Make session.end omit cost_usd when the run cost is unknown, update session event/replay types to distinguish omitted cost from zero-cost local runs, and replace the current session-end assertion with regression coverage for both known-cost and unknown-cost sessions.\",\"id\":\"hx-cce583e1\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"helix\",\"phase:build\",\"review-finding\"],\"owner\":\"erik\",\"priority\":0,\"spec-id\":\"loop.go\",\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"correctness: session.end still emits unknown cost as numeric sentinel\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-09T22:14:59.058088662Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:382:{\"acceptance\":\"A session whose chat spans all have known cost preserves a root invoke_agent ddx.cost.amount equal to the sum of child costs even when provenance differs across turns; the root span only emits ddx.cost.source=unknown when at least one contributing chat span has unknown cost; automated tests cover mixed provider-reported/configured cost rollups.\",\"claimed-at\":\"2026-04-10T04:41:54Z\",\"claimed-machine\":\"eitri\",\"claimed-pid\":\"615913\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"421f59e695319df41a2ec9016b13f652cb98ed6e\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-10T04:22:39.474002339Z\",\"description\":\"Review finding from fresh-eyes review.\\nFile: loop.go:289\\nCategory: correctness\\nSeverity: medium\\nDescription: The last commit's root-span cost rollup logic marks the invoke_agent span as unknown whenever known child chat spans disagree on ddx.cost.source, currency, or pricing_ref. That discards a valid session total even though every contributing chat span has known cost, which conflicts with FEAT-005 requirement 22, ADR-001's known-vs-unknown cost policy, and CONTRACT-001's rule that the root rollup only becomes unknown when a contributing chat span has unknown cost. In the committed code, a two-turn session with one provider-reported attempt and one exact configured-cost attempt yields result.CostUSD=0.03 while applySessionCostAttributes still emits root ddx.cost.source=unknown because sessionCostStable became false.\\nSuggested fix: Preserve root ddx.cost.amount whenever every contributing chat span has known cost, and only force ddx.cost.source=unknown when a contributing span is actually unknown. If source/currency/pricing_ref cannot be represented cleanly for mixed provenance, omit or summarize those metadata fields instead of discarding the known total. Add regression coverage for mixed provider-reported plus configured-cost sessions.\",\"id\":\"hx-d2c7ec7e\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"helix\",\"phase:build\",\"review-finding\"],\"notes\":\"Superseded by commit `421f59e695319df41a2ec9016b13f652cb98ed6e` (`hx-cacc76f6 preserve mixed-provenance root cost amount`).\\n\\nThe root invoke_agent span now preserves `ddx.cost.amount` for mixed known-cost sessions and the regression coverage for mixed provider-reported plus configured-cost rollups is in `loop_test.go`.\",\"owner\":\"erik\",\"priority\":0,\"spec-id\":\"loop.go\",\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"correctness: mixed known-cost root rollups must stay known\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-10T04:42:13.284855944Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:383:{\"acceptance\":\"Streaming chat spans measure ddx.timing.first_token_ms from before ChatStream is invoked; a test with a provider whose ChatStream blocks before yielding output includes 