{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git show HEAD:docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-003-ddx-agent-service.md | nl -ba | sed -n '1,320p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# CONTRACT-003: DdxAgent Service Interface\n     2\t\n     3\t**Status:** Draft\n     4\t**Owner:** DDX Agent maintainers\n     5\t**Replaces:** CONTRACT-002-ddx-harness-interface (deleted; entanglement-era contract)\n     6\t\n     7\t## Purpose\n     8\t\n     9\tThis contract defines the **entire public Go surface** of the `ddx-agent` module.\n    10\tAnything not reachable through the `DdxAgent` interface — or through the input/output\n    11\tstruct types referenced by its methods — is internal and may change without notice.\n    12\t\n    13\tConsumers (DDx CLI, future HELIX/Dun integrations, the standalone `ddx-agent`\n    14\tbinary, anything else) interact only through this surface. **They do not import\n    15\tagent internal packages.** When new behavior is needed, consumers file an issue or\n    16\tPR against this contract; agent maintainers decide whether the surface grows.\n    17\t\n    18\t## Module value proposition\n    19\t\n    20\t`ddx-agent` is the one stop shop for optimally routed one-shot noninteractive\n    21\tagentic prompts. Two roles:\n    22\t\n    23\t1. **Direct first-class agent** over native model providers (LM Studio, OpenRouter,\n    24\t   Anthropic, etc.). Designed to be the high-performance choice for batch\n    25\t   noninteractive tasks.\n    26\t2. **Wrapper around other agents** — subprocess harnesses (claude, codex,\n    27\t   opencode, pi, gemini) — used when their interactive features, vendor billing,\n    28\t   specific capabilities, or comparison/fallback routing wants them in the\n    29\t   candidate pool.\n    30\t\n    31\tA single internal routing engine ranks `(harness, provider?, model)` candidates\n    32\tuniformly. Consumers see one surface; the internals decide how to dispatch.\n    33\t\n    34\t## Interface\n    35\t\n    36\t```go\n    37\tpackage agentlib\n    38\t\n    39\timport (\n    40\t    \"context\"\n    41\t    \"io\"\n    42\t    \"time\"\n    43\t    \"encoding/json\"\n    44\t)\n    45\t\n    46\t// DdxAgent is the entire public Go surface of the ddx-agent module.\n    47\ttype DdxAgent interface {\n    48\t    // Execute runs an agent task in-process; emits Events on the channel until\n    49\t    // the task terminates (channel closes). The final event (type=final) carries\n    50\t    // status, usage, cost, session log path, optional message history, and\n    51\t    // routing_actual (the resolved fallback chain that fired).\n    52\t    Execute(ctx context.Context, req ExecuteRequest) (<-chan Event, error)\n    53\t\n    54\t    // TailSessionLog streams events from a previously-started or in-progress\n    55\t    // session by ID. Used by clients (DDx workers, UIs) to subscribe to a run\n    56\t    // started elsewhere — e.g., a server-managed worker that the CLI wants to\n    57\t    // follow. Multi-subscriber-safe.\n    58\t    TailSessionLog(ctx context.Context, sessionID string) (<-chan Event, error)\n    59\t\n    60\t    // ListHarnesses returns metadata for every registered harness (native and\n    61\t    // subprocess). HarnessInfo includes install state, supported permission\n    62\t    // levels, supported reasoning values, and live quota when applicable.\n    63\t    ListHarnesses(ctx context.Context) ([]HarnessInfo, error)\n    64\t\n    65\t    // ListProviders returns providers known to the native-agent harness with\n    66\t    // live status, configured-default markers, and cooldown state.\n    67\t    ListProviders(ctx context.Context) ([]ProviderInfo, error)\n    68\t\n    69\t    // ListModels returns models matching the filter, with full metadata\n    70\t    // (cost, perf signals, capabilities, context length, ranking).\n    71\t    ListModels(ctx context.Context, filter ModelFilter) ([]ModelInfo, error)\n    72\t\n    73\t    // HealthCheck triggers a fresh probe and updates internal state.\n    74\t    // Target.Type is \"harness\" or \"provider\".\n    75\t    HealthCheck(ctx context.Context, target HealthTarget) error\n    76\t\n    77\t    // ResolveRoute resolves a single under-specified request to a concrete\n    78\t    // (Harness, Provider, Model). The returned RouteDecision can be passed\n    79\t    // back to Execute via ExecuteRequest.PreResolved to skip re-resolution\n    80\t    // (used by dry-run-then-execute flows).\n    81\t    ResolveRoute(ctx context.Context, req RouteRequest) (*RouteDecision, error)\n    82\t\n    83\t    // RouteStatus returns global routing state across all routes: cooldowns,\n    84\t    // recent decisions, observation-derived per-(provider,model) latency.\n    85\t    // Distinct from per-request ResolveRoute — this is the read-only operator\n    86\t    // dashboard view.\n    87\t    RouteStatus(ctx context.Context) (*RouteStatusReport, error)\n    88\t}\n    89\t\n    90\t// New constructs a DdxAgent. Options is intentionally minimal.\n    91\tfunc New(opts Options) (DdxAgent, error)\n    92\t```\n    93\t\n    94\t**Eight methods total.** `Execute` is the primary verb; `TailSessionLog`,\n    95\t`ListHarnesses`, `ListProviders`, `ListModels`, `HealthCheck`, `ResolveRoute`,\n    96\t`RouteStatus` are the supporting surface. (Counted as \"7 + New\" in earlier\n    97\tdrafts; interface has 8 methods.)\n    98\t\n    99\t## Public types\n   100\t\n   101\t```go\n   102\ttype Options struct {\n   103\t    ConfigPath string    // optional override; default $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ddx-agent/config.yaml\n   104\t    Logger     io.Writer // optional; agent writes structured session logs internally regardless\n   105\t\n   106\t    // Test-only injection seams. Each MUST be nil in production builds —\n   107\t    // enforced by build tag `//go:build testseam`. Forming an Options with\n   108\t    // any of these set in a non-test build is a compile error. Four seams\n   109\t    // exist because consumers today inject at four different layers.\n   110\t    FakeProvider            *FakeProvider\n   111\t    PromptAssertionHook     PromptAssertionHook\n   112\t    CompactionAssertionHook CompactionAssertionHook\n   113\t    ToolWiringHook          ToolWiringHook\n   114\t}\n   115\t\n   116\t// Reasoning is the single public model-reasoning control. It is one scalar:\n   117\t// named values such as auto/off/low/medium/high/minimal/xhigh/max, or numeric\n   118\t// strings produced by ReasoningTokens for explicit token budgets.\n   119\t//\n   120\t// The root package may re-export this type, constants, and helper from a shared\n   121\t// leaf package such as internal/reasoning. Internal packages such as\n   122\t// internal/modelcatalog import the leaf package, not root agent, to avoid\n   123\t// root-agent/internal-modelcatalog import cycles.\n   124\ttype Reasoning string\n   125\t\n   126\tconst (\n   127\t    ReasoningAuto   Reasoning = \"auto\"\n   128\t    ReasoningOff    Reasoning = \"off\"\n   129\t    ReasoningLow    Reasoning = \"low\"\n   130\t    ReasoningMedium Reasoning = \"medium\"\n   131\t    ReasoningHigh   Reasoning = \"high\"\n   132\t    ReasoningMinimal Reasoning = \"minimal\" // accepted only when advertised\n   133\t    ReasoningXHigh  Reasoning = \"xhigh\"    // normalizes x-high\n   134\t    ReasoningMax    Reasoning = \"max\"      // requires known model/provider max\n   135\t)\n   136\t\n   137\tfunc ReasoningTokens(n int) Reasoning\n   138\t\n   139\ttype ExecuteRequest struct {\n   140\t    Prompt       string  // required\n   141\t    SystemPrompt string  // optional; agent supplies a sane default if empty\n   142\t    Model        string  // optional; resolved via ResolveRoute if empty\n   143\t    Provider     string  // optional preference (soft); empty = router decides\n   144\t    Harness      string  // optional preference (hard); empty = router decides\n   145\t    ModelRef     string  // optional alias from the catalog: cheap/standard/smart/<custom>\n   146\t    Temperature  float32 // model sampling temperature; 0 = deterministic\n   147\t    Seed         int64   // sampling seed; 0 = unset/provider chooses\n   148\t    Reasoning    Reasoning // optional; auto|off|low|medium|high|minimal|xhigh|max|<tokens>\n   149\t    Permissions  string  // \"safe\" | \"supervised\" | \"unrestricted\"; default \"safe\"\n   150\t    WorkDir      string  // required when the chosen harness uses tools\n   151\t\n   152\t    // PreResolved bypasses ResolveRoute when the caller already has a decision\n   153\t    // (e.g., from a prior ResolveRoute call). When non-nil, agent uses these\n   154\t    // values verbatim and does not re-route. Provider/Model/Harness fields\n   155\t    // above are ignored in this mode.\n   156\t    PreResolved *RouteDecision\n   157\t\n   158\t    // Three independent timeout knobs:\n   159\t    //   Timeout         — wall-clock cap; the request fails after this duration\n   160\t    //                     regardless of activity. 0 = no cap.\n   161\t    //   IdleTimeout     — streaming-quiet cap; the request fails after this\n   162\t    //                     duration of no events from the model. 0 = use harness\n   163\t    //                     default (typically 60s).\n   164\t    //   ProviderTimeout — per-HTTP-request cap to the provider; longer requests\n   165\t    //                     are retried per the harness's failover rules. 0 = use\n   166\t    //                     provider default.\n   167\t    Timeout         time.Duration\n   168\t    IdleTimeout     time.Duration\n   169\t    ProviderTimeout time.Duration\n   170\t\n   171\t    // Optional stall policy. When non-nil, agent enforces and ends execution\n   172\t    // with Status=\"stalled\" if any limit hits. The agent also derives an\n   173\t    // implicit MaxIterations ceiling from StallPolicy (typically 2× the\n   174\t    // ReadOnly limit) — caller does not configure MaxIterations directly.\n   175\t    StallPolicy *StallPolicy\n   176\t\n   177\t    // SessionLogDir overrides the default session-log directory for this\n   178\t    // request. Used by execute-bead to direct logs into a per-bundle evidence\n   179\t    // directory. Empty = use Options.ConfigPath-derived default.\n   180\t    SessionLogDir string\n   181\t\n   182\t    // Metadata is bidirectional: echoed back in every Event via Event.Metadata,\n   183\t    // AND stamped onto every line written to the session log (e.g., bead_id,\n   184\t    // attempt_id) so external log consumers can correlate.\n   185\t    Metadata map[string]string\n   186\t}\n   187\t\n   188\ttype StallPolicy struct {\n   189\t    MaxReadOnlyToolIterations int // 0 = disabled\n   190\t    MaxNoopCompactions        int // 0 = disabled\n   191\t}\n   192\t\n   193\ttype RouteRequest struct {\n   194\t    Model       string\n   195\t    Provider    string\n   196\t    Harness     string\n   197\t    ModelRef    string\n   198\t    Reasoning   Reasoning\n   199\t    Permissions string\n   200\t}\n   201\t\n   202\ttype RouteDecision struct {\n   203\t    Harness    string\n   204\t    Provider   string  // empty for harnesses without provider concept\n   205\t    Model      string\n   206\t    Reason     string  // human-readable explanation\n   207\t    Candidates []Candidate  // full ranking, including rejected candidates\n   208\t}\n   209\t\n   210\ttype Candidate struct {\n   211\t    Harness       string\n   212\t    Provider      string\n   213\t    Model         string\n   214\t    Score         float64\n   215\t    Eligible      bool\n   216\t    Reason        string\n   217\t    EstimatedCost CostEstimate\n   218\t    PerfSignal    PerfSignal\n   219\t}\n   220\t\n   221\ttype HarnessInfo struct {\n   222\t    Name                 string\n   223\t    Type                 string   // \"native\" | \"subprocess\"\n   224\t    Available            bool\n   225\t    Path                 string   // for subprocess harnesses\n   226\t    Error                string   // when Available=false\n   227\t    IsLocal              bool\n   228\t    IsSubscription       bool\n   229\t    ExactPinSupport      bool\n   230\t    DefaultModel         string   // built-in default model when no override is supplied\n   231\t    SupportedPermissions []string // subset of {\"safe\",\"supervised\",\"unrestricted\"}\n   232\t    SupportedReasoning   []string // values such as {\"off\",\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\",\"minimal\",\"xhigh\",\"max\"}\n   233\t    CostClass            string   // \"local\" | \"cheap\" | \"medium\" | \"expensive\"\n   234\t    Quota                *QuotaState // nil if not applicable; live field\n   235\t}\n   236\t\n   237\ttype ProviderInfo struct {\n   238\t    Name          string\n   239\t    Type          string  // \"openai-compat\" | \"anthropic\" | \"virtual\"\n   240\t    BaseURL       string\n   241\t    Status        string  // \"connected\" | \"unreachable\" | \"error: <msg>\"\n   242\t    ModelCount    int\n   243\t    Capabilities  []string  // {\"tool_use\",\"vision\",\"json_mode\",\"streaming\"}\n   244\t    IsDefault     bool      // matches the configured default_provider\n   245\t    DefaultModel  string    // the per-provider configured default model, if any\n   246\t    CooldownState *CooldownState  // nil if not in cooldown\n   247\t}\n   248\t\n   249\ttype ModelInfo struct {\n   250\t    ID            string\n   251\t    Provider      string\n   252\t    Harness       string  // for subprocess-only models, the owning harness\n   253\t    ContextLength int     // resolved (provider API > catalog > default)\n   254\t    Capabilities  []string\n   255\t    Cost          CostInfo\n   256\t    PerfSignal    PerfSignal\n   257\t    Available     bool\n   258\t    IsConfigured  bool    // matches an explicit model_routes entry\n   259\t    IsDefault     bool    // matches the configured default model\n   260\t    CatalogRef    string  // canonical catalog reference if recognized\n   261\t    ReasoningDefault Reasoning // catalog/provider default for this model, if known\n   262\t    ReasoningMaxTokens int     // 0 when unknown or not applicable\n   263\t    RankPosition  int     // ordinal in the latest discovery rank for this provider; -1 if unranked\n   264\t}\n   265\t\n   266\ttype ModelFilter struct {\n   267\t    Harness  string  // empty = all harnesses\n   268\t    Provider string  // empty = all providers\n   269\t}\n   270\t\n   271\ttype HealthTarget struct {\n   272\t    Type string  // \"harness\" | \"provider\"\n   273\t    Name string\n   274\t}\n   275\t\n   276\ttype CooldownState struct {\n   277\t    Reason    string    // \"consecutive_failures\" | \"manual\" | etc.\n   278\t    Until     time.Time\n   279\t    FailCount int\n   280\t    LastError string\n   281\t}\n   282\t\n   283\ttype RouteStatusReport struct {\n   284\t    Routes          []RouteStatusEntry\n   285\t    GeneratedAt     time.Time\n   286\t    GlobalCooldowns []CooldownState\n   287\t}\n   288\t\n   289\ttype RouteStatusEntry struct {\n   290\t    Model          string                  // route key\n   291\t    Strategy       string                  // \"priority-round-robin\" | \"first-available\"\n   292\t    Candidates     []RouteCandidateStatus\n   293\t    LastDecision   *RouteDecision          // most recent ResolveRoute result for this key (cached)\n   294\t    LastDecisionAt time.Time\n   295\t}\n   296\t\n   297\ttype RouteCandidateStatus struct {\n   298\t    Provider          string\n   299\t    Model             string\n   300\t    Priority          int\n   301\t    Healthy           bool\n   302\t    Cooldown          *CooldownState\n   303\t    RecentLatencyMS   float64  // observation-derived\n   304\t    RecentSuccessRate float64  // 0-1\n   305\t}\n   306\t\n   307\ttype Event struct {\n   308\t    Type     string          // see event types below\n   309\t    Sequence int64\n   310\t    Time     time.Time\n   311\t    Metadata map[string]string  // echoed from ExecuteRequest.Metadata\n   312\t    Data     json.RawMessage    // shape depends on Type; see schemas below\n   313\t}\n   314\t```\n   315\t\n   316\t## Event JSON shapes\n   317\t\n   318\tClosed union of event types. Every harness backend emits these identically.\n   319\t\n   320\t```jsonc\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
