27756\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"1b6047e671e540a25ff37d20782d1bfba6d0ae78\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-10T01:31:14.682184831Z\",\"description\":\"\\u003ccontext-digest\\u003eRepo-wide HELIX alignment review on 2026-04-09 after usage-reporting, symlink-resolution, CI-gate, and telemetry changes. Scope areas: runtime/replay, tools/path semantics, CLI/structured I/O/usage/continuity, telemetry/streaming. Active concerns: go-std, testing.\\u003c/context-digest\\u003e\\nTop-down reconciliation review for repository scope.\\nScope areas: runtime/replay, tools/path semantics, CLI/structured I/O/usage/continuity, telemetry/streaming.\\nGoverning artifacts: docs/helix/00-discover/product-vision.md; docs/helix/01-frame/prd.md; docs/helix/01-frame/features/FEAT-001..007; docs/helix/02-design/architecture.md; docs/helix/02-design/solution-designs/SD-001..006; docs/helix/02-design/adr/ADR-001-observability-surfaces-and-cost-attribution.md; docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-001-otel-telemetry-capture.md.\",\"id\":\"hx-76f94627\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"helix\",\"kind:planning\",\"action:align\"],\"owner\":\"erik\",\"priority\":0,\"spec-id\":\"docs/helix/01-frame/prd.md\",\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"align: repo\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-10T01:35:42.538807159Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:336:{\"acceptance\":\"CONTRACT-001 explicitly defines how the root invoke_agent span represents known session totals when child chat spans have mixed known provenance; the contract no longer requires an impossible or ambiguous ddx.cost.source/pricing_ref combination at the root; conformance tests or checklist coverage include a mixed provider-reported/configured session example.\",\"claimed-at\":\"2026-04-10T04:23:38Z\",\"claimed-machine\":\"eitri\",\"claimed-pid\":\"547576\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"c083df5f46fe37557b8feedf66af32013a0a9e35\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-10T04:15:39.179486428Z\",\"description\":\"Review finding from fresh-eyes review.\\nFile: docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-001-otel-telemetry-capture.md:221\\nCategory: correctness\\nSeverity: medium\\nDescription: CONTRACT-001 says the root invoke_agent span should emit a session cost rollup whenever every contributing chat span has known cost, and only become unknown when any child cost is unknown. But the contract never defines what ddx.cost.source, ddx.cost.currency, and ddx.cost.pricing_ref should look like when all child chat costs are known yet their provenance differs across turns, such as one provider-reported turn plus one configured-cost turn. That makes the required root shape ambiguous: ddx.cost.source is required when amount is known, but the allowed enum only models single-attempt provenance. The current implementation fell into this gap and downgraded a known total to unknown when provenance metadata differed.\\nSuggested fix: Amend the root-span cost-rollup section to specify a conformant representation for mixed known-cost provenance. Either add an explicit aggregate/root rollup source shape, or state that the root may still emit ddx.cost.amount and currency while omitting or summarizing provenance fields that cannot be represented cleanly. Add a contract-focused regression test or checklist entry covering mixed provider-reported/configured sessions.\",\"id\":\"hx-7853958b\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"helix\",\"phase:build\",\"review-finding\"],\"owner\":\"erik\",\"priority\":0,\"spec-id\":\"docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-001-otel-telemetry-capture.md\",\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"correctness: define mixed-provenance root cost rollup semantics\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-10T04:24:48.231802016Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:341:{\"acceptance\":\"All review passes complete; findings filed as beads; AGENTS.md updated if needed\",\"claimed-at\":\"2026-04-10T00:29:51Z\",\"claimed-machine\":\"eitri\",\"claimed-pid\":\"3426874\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"57e3978600fbc45e4cd40e13a63fb76bde456676\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-10T00:29:46.902427804Z\",\"description\":\"\\u003ccontext-digest\\u003e\\n\\u003cprinciples\\u003eDesign for Change · Design for Simplicity · Validate Your Work · Make Intent Explicit · Prefer Reversible Decisions\\u003c/principles\\u003e\\n\\u003cconcerns\\u003ego-std | testing\\u003c/concerns\\u003e\\n\\u003cpractices\\u003ego fmt ./... before every commit · go test ./... and go test -race ./... for concurrent code · golangci-lint run · gosec ./... · govulncheck ./... · log with slog, wrap errors with context, and keep tests table-driven with testify\\u003c/practices\\u003e\\n\\u003cadrs\\u003eADR-001 keeps JSONL replay separate from OTel analytics, preserves reported cost when available, uses exact runtime pricing only for known systems/models, and leaves cost unknown otherwise so replay fidelity and cross-tool analytics both survive.\\u003c/adrs\\u003e\\n\\u003cgoverning\\u003eCONTRACT-001 root span scaffolding — review last commit 57e3978600fbc45e4cd40e13a63fb76bde456676 for telemetry package correctness, concern compliance, and follow-on work.\\u003c/governing\\u003e\\n\\u003c/context-digest\\u003e\\n\\nFresh-eyes review of last-commit telemetry scaffolding.\\nReview target: last-commit\\nReviewed implementation bead: agent-bb6aad8a\\nReviewed spec: docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-001-otel-telemetry-capture.md\",\"id\":\"hx-86591e1a\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"helix\",\"kind:planning\",\"action:review\"],\"notes\":\"\\u003cmeasure-results\\u003e\\n  \\u003ctimestamp\\u003e2026-04-10T00:33:12Z\\u003c/timestamp\\u003e\\n  \\u003cstatus\\u003ePARTIAL\\u003c/status\\u003e\\n  \\u003cfindings total='1' filed='1' critical='0' high='0' medium='1' low='0'/\\u003e\\n  \\u003cagents-md-updated\\u003eYES\\u003c/agents-md-updated\\u003e\\n  \\u003clearnings-filed\\u003e0\\u003c/learnings-filed\\u003e\\n  \\u003cacceptance\\u003e\\n    \\u003ccriterion name='all review passes complete' status='pass' evidence='Reviewed commit 57e3978600fbc45e4cd40e13a63fb76bde456676 across correctness, integration, concern-aware quality, and operational learnings passes.'/\\u003e\\n    \\u003ccriterion name='findings filed as beads' status='pass' evidence='Filed review-finding bead hx-b33b6243.'/\\u003e\\n    \\u003ccriterion name='AGENTS.md updated if needed' status='pass' evidence='Updated AGENTS.md package layout to document telemetry/.'/\\u003e\\n  \\u003c/acceptance\\u003e\\n  \\u003cgates\\u003e\\n    \\u003cgate concern='go-std' command='go test ./...' status='pass'/\\u003e\\n    \\u003cgate concern='go-std' command='go vet ./...' status='pass'/\\u003e\\n    \\u003cgate concern='go-std' command='golangci-lint run ./telemetry/...' status='pass'/\\u003e\\n    \\u003cgate concern='go-std' command='gosec ./telemetry/...' status='pass'/\\u003e\\n    \\u003cgate concern='go-std' command='go test -race ./...' status='fail'/\\u003e\\n    \\u003cgate concern='go-std' command='govulncheck ./telemetry/...' status='fail'/\\u003e\\n  \\u003c/gates\\u003e\\n  \\u003cnote\\u003eMeasure status is PARTIAL because go test -race ./... could not run with CGO disabled in this environment, and the installed govulncheck binary was built against Go 1.25 while the repository requires Go 1.26.1.\\u003c/note\\u003e\\n\\u003c/measure-results\\u003e\",\"owner\":\"erik\",\"priority\":0,\"spec-id\":\"57e3978600fbc45e4cd40e13a63fb76bde456676\",\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"review: last-commit 57e3978 telemetry scaffolding\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-10T00:33:25.244298649Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:345:{\"acceptance\":\"Streaming chat spans measure ddx.timing.first_token_ms from the same timestamp used to start the chat span; a test with a blocking EventLLMRequest callback and a streaming provider confirms first_token_ms includes callback delay before ChatStream begins.\",\"claimed-at\":\"2026-04-10T01:18:48Z\",\"claimed-machine\":\"eitri\",\"claimed-pid\":\"3894095\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"4df0f7e92c3f685d9843714ab7b10e5a4a04741e\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-10T01:17:28.821747551Z\",\"description\":\"Review finding from fresh-eyes review.\\nFile: loop.go:175\\nCategory: correctness\\nSeverity: medium\\nDescription: Commit 4df0f7e moved `streamStart` earlier inside `consumeStream`, but `ddx.timing.first_token_ms` is still measured after the chat span starts. `Run` starts the `chat` span at loop.go:175, then emits `EventLLMRequest` before calling `consumeStream`; because callbacks are user-supplied and can block, the exported attribute can still under-report first-token latency by the callback time and therefore violate CONTRACT-001's requirement that the value measure from span start to first streamed token.\\nSuggested fix: Capture the chat span/request start timestamp in `Run` and thread it into `consumeStream` so `Attempt.Timing.FirstToken` is derived from the same timestamp that anchors the `chat` span. Add an end-to-end test where the request callback sleeps before streaming begins and assert the chat span's `ddx.timing.first_token_ms` includes that delay.\",\"id\":\"hx-8bf6ee3a\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"helix\",\"phase:build\",\"review-finding\",\"area:lib\"],\"owner\":\"erik\",\"priority\":0,\"spec-id\":\"loop.go\",\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"correctness: first_token_ms still excludes pre-stream callback latency\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-10T01:19:57.86077717Z\"}\nHEAD:.ddx/beads.jsonl:346:{\"acceptance\":\"All review passes complete; findings filed as beads; AGENTS.md updated if needed\",\"closing_commit_sha\":\"421f59e695319df41a2ec9016b13f652cb98ed6e\",\"created_at\":\"2026-04-10T04:36:43.923143107Z\",\"description\":\"\\u003ccontext-digest\\u003e\\n\\u003cprinciples\\u003eDesign for Change · Design for Simplicity · Validate Your Work · Make Intent Explicit · Prefer Reversible Decisions\\u003c/principles\\u003e\\n\\u003cconcerns\\u003ego-std | testing\\u003c/concerns\\u003e\\n\\u003cpractices\\u003eUse Go stdlib toolchain, testing stdlib with testify assertions, and preserve deterministic verificatio