eStream still timestamps the first output only after emitting EventLLMDelta. Because emitCallback is user-supplied and can block, a slow llm.delta callback will still inflate ddx.timing.first_token_ms and ddx.timing.generation_ms, which violates CONTRACT-001s requirement that timing reflect span-to-token and generation windows rather than observer latency.\\nSuggested fix: Capture the arrival timestamp for each delta before invoking the callback, use that pre-callback timestamp for the first output boundary and generation window math, and add a regression test where an EventLLMDelta callback sleeps while the first streamed delta arrives.\",\"id\":\"hx-fd626e74\",\"issue_type\":\"task\",\"labels\":[\"helix\",\"phase:build\",\"review-finding\"],\"owner\":\"erik\",\"priority\":0,\"spec-id\":\"docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-001-otel-telemetry-capture.md\",\"status\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"correctness: first_token_ms still counts blocking llm.delta callbacks\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-04-10T01:38:50.580711052Z\"}\nHEAD:docs/helix/01-frame/features/FEAT-005-logging-and-cost.md:89:    `docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-001-otel-telemetry-capture.md`.\nHEAD:docs/helix/01-frame/features/FEAT-005-logging-and-cost.md:170:| AC-FEAT-005-04 | OTel export conforms to `CONTRACT-001`, including span taxonomy, identity fields, cost/timing attributes, tool error semantics, and throughput formulas derived only from valid timing windows. | `go test ./telemetry ./...` |\nHEAD:docs/helix/01-frame/features/FEAT-005-logging-and-cost.md:181:- `CONTRACT-001` is authoritative for telemetry field names, formulas, and\nHEAD:docs/helix/02-design/adr/ADR-001-observability-surfaces-and-cost-attribution.md:40:`docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-001-otel-telemetry-capture.md`.\nHEAD:docs/helix/02-design/adr/ADR-001-observability-surfaces-and-cost-attribution.md:96:- [CONTRACT-001 OTel Telemetry Capture](/Users/erik/Projects/agent/docs/helix/02-design/contracts/CONTRACT-001-otel-telem